# iCloud/cloud-sync conflict copies, e.g. "file 2.ext" / "file 3.ext".
#
# This ENUMERATED 2/3/4 until 2026-08-27, by which point the copies had reached
# 7: 48 files, 4.6MB, untracked in public/downloads/ and noise in every
# `git status`. None were ever tracked, so none ever shipped — the cost was
# attention, not bandwidth. A range covers whatever number the next one picks.
#
# It deliberately starts at 2, NOT 1. A sync conflict is by definition a SECOND
# copy, and a [0-9] class would have swallowed two real files that merely look
# like one: "product picture/Palette Pack Vol. 1.png" and
# "colorarchive_logo_v1_assets/screenshot website 1.png".
#
# These are conflict copies, not build output: scripts/generate-downloads.mjs
# only ever writes canonical names. Deleting them does not need a rebuild.
**/* [2-9].*
**/* [1-9][0-9].*
# ...but keep these legitimately-numbered files that resemble conflict copies
!colorarchive_logo_v1_assets/screenshot website 2.png
!colorarchive_logo_v1_assets/screenshot website 3.png
